WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.583
(joyful music)

00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:08.063
(joyful music)

00:00:10.007 --> 00:00:12.150
- I was so nervous for some reason.

00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:13.650
- Please don't show how much I sweat

00:00:13.650 --> 00:00:16.170
without showing how much
they put me through.

00:00:16.170 --> 00:00:17.400
I thought I was gonna get here

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:19.140
and lift the bar one time.

00:00:19.140 --> 00:00:21.450
That's not what happened, whatsoever.

00:00:21.450 --> 00:00:22.860
- I mean, we're extremely strong.

00:00:22.860 --> 00:00:23.970
We're animals, right?

00:00:23.970 --> 00:00:26.168
- Strong chicken legs. (laughs)

00:00:26.168 --> 00:00:27.001
- Cluck cluck.

00:00:27.001 --> 00:00:28.418
(laughter)

00:00:28.418 --> 00:00:30.690
(clucking chickens)

00:00:30.690 --> 00:00:33.030
- Really quickly, what do you guys do,

00:00:33.030 --> 00:00:33.863
on the day to day,

00:00:33.863 --> 00:00:35.217
to stay healthy and work out?

00:00:35.217 --> 00:00:36.867
- I'm really into supplements.

00:00:36.867 --> 00:00:39.660
and I like spirulina blue-green algae,

00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:42.660
but I just go to 24 hour
fitness. I don't anything crazy.

00:00:42.660 --> 00:00:46.440
- I am a PhD student and
a professional sprinter.

00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:48.103
- I'm like, "Go over there."

00:00:48.103 --> 00:00:49.050
- (laughter)

00:00:49.050 --> 00:00:50.370
- But, there's like a big
difference I feel like,

00:00:50.370 --> 00:00:52.470
between lifting for sprinting.

00:00:52.470 --> 00:00:54.600
And then it sounds like
a lot of y'all, like,

00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:56.140
lift for lifting and I...

00:00:56.140 --> 00:00:58.200
- Is lifting like a regular
part of your training?

00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:01.050
- Yeah, we lift like two
to three days a week.

00:01:01.050 --> 00:01:02.040
- That counts.

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:03.043
- Yeah.

00:01:03.043 --> 00:01:03.876
(laughter)

00:01:03.876 --> 00:01:04.709
- More than me.

00:01:04.709 --> 00:01:05.542
- I have a cerebral palsy, yeah.

00:01:05.542 --> 00:01:07.680
So, I run for the US Paralympics.

00:01:07.680 --> 00:01:09.930
For so long, I shied away
from things that I thought

00:01:09.930 --> 00:01:11.970
would be too hard
because of my disability,

00:01:11.970 --> 00:01:14.880
but then, the more that I
got into running and lifting,

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:17.018
the more I was like, "No,"
like, "I can do these things,

00:01:17.018 --> 00:01:18.780
Just as well as everyone else."

00:01:18.780 --> 00:01:19.613
- What about you?

00:01:19.613 --> 00:01:22.020
- I've been lifting for about
10 years, but I would say,

00:01:22.020 --> 00:01:25.350
between 2012 and 2016,

00:01:25.350 --> 00:01:27.210
that's when I was really intense about it.

00:01:27.210 --> 00:01:31.140
But nowadays, I could
work out six days a week.

00:01:31.140 --> 00:01:33.150
Sometimes, I don't work out at all.

00:01:33.150 --> 00:01:34.920
- Well, because of your history,

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:35.760
I feel like you should go...

00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:36.593
- I know.

00:01:36.593 --> 00:01:37.426
- So, we can just...

00:01:38.323 --> 00:01:40.020
- Shift down this way.

00:01:40.020 --> 00:01:41.170
I'll just go down here.

00:01:42.141 --> 00:01:43.290
- Please, please.

00:01:43.290 --> 00:01:45.840
- Okay, I feel like I
should at least be right...

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:46.673
- After the sprinter.

00:01:46.673 --> 00:01:48.177
- No

00:01:48.177 --> 00:01:49.010
(laughter)

00:01:49.010 --> 00:01:50.763
- And, you lift come up here.

00:01:51.751 --> 00:01:53.054
(laughter)

00:01:53.054 --> 00:01:54.508
- Okay, hold on.

00:01:54.508 --> 00:01:55.915
(giggling)

00:01:55.915 --> 00:01:58.470
- Yeah, I feel like, EMTs have
to be able to lift people.

00:01:58.470 --> 00:02:00.141
- That's right, that's right.

00:02:00.141 --> 00:02:01.230
- Okay.

00:02:01.230 --> 00:02:02.797
We do have the fire
department, so, I always say,

00:02:02.797 --> 00:02:04.967
"Lift with your fire
department, not your backs."

00:02:06.182 --> 00:02:07.015
but I will say...

00:02:07.015 --> 00:02:08.269
yeah, I think I... I check...

00:02:08.269 --> 00:02:09.930
I think I do 10,000 steps per shift.

00:02:09.930 --> 00:02:11.280
I work 911 in Albuquerque.

00:02:11.280 --> 00:02:12.600
We're a pretty busy system.

00:02:12.600 --> 00:02:15.390
And I have had to pick
up people off the ground.

00:02:15.390 --> 00:02:17.880
Where it's just me and my partner.

00:02:17.880 --> 00:02:20.340
But look, look, look guys, guys....

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:21.570
Listen, okay.

00:02:21.570 --> 00:02:23.460
There's adrenaline involved, you know?

00:02:23.460 --> 00:02:25.470
But, right now, I'm here and sweaty,

00:02:25.470 --> 00:02:26.440
so I don't really think it's
going to the same scenario.

00:02:26.440 --> 00:02:29.370
- I'm so sweaty. We haven't
started lifting yet.

00:02:29.370 --> 00:02:30.990
- Do you kinda, wanna...

00:02:30.990 --> 00:02:33.210
Give a little description
on how we started lifting?

00:02:33.210 --> 00:02:36.190
- I'll go first, so I
don't lift whatsoever.

00:02:36.190 --> 00:02:37.830
I actually... I do exercise though.

00:02:37.830 --> 00:02:40.012
I do boxing and I go...

00:02:40.012 --> 00:02:42.870
(excited chattering)

00:02:42.870 --> 00:02:44.730
But, that has nothing to
do with weight training.

00:02:44.730 --> 00:02:47.490
Which is why, I feel, I
should be more this way.

00:02:47.490 --> 00:02:48.323
- Okay, okay.

00:02:48.323 --> 00:02:49.556
- Still strong though.

00:02:49.556 --> 00:02:50.970
- I feel like you have that explosiveness.

00:02:50.970 --> 00:02:51.803
- I know.

00:02:51.803 --> 00:02:53.277
(understanding mumbles)

00:02:53.277 --> 00:02:54.300
- A little pump, here and there.

00:02:54.300 --> 00:02:57.120
- I got into lifting when
I started doing track.

00:02:57.120 --> 00:03:00.660
I randomly started in two
of the weirdest events.

00:03:00.660 --> 00:03:02.940
Pole vault and javelin in high school.

00:03:02.940 --> 00:03:05.910
And the guy who coached both those events

00:03:05.910 --> 00:03:08.370
he had this program
called, "Six Week Freak."

00:03:08.370 --> 00:03:10.320
Where between the...

00:03:10.320 --> 00:03:11.250
- That's kinda nasty.

00:03:11.250 --> 00:03:13.590
Right? I was like, "Damn, we are 16!"

00:03:13.590 --> 00:03:15.049
- Like a Meg Thee Stallion song. (giggles)

00:03:15.049 --> 00:03:17.070
- But, it was like a six
week program where we focused

00:03:17.070 --> 00:03:18.990
on like three main Olympic lifts.

00:03:18.990 --> 00:03:20.670
And I was like, "Oh, this is so cool,

00:03:20.670 --> 00:03:23.430
it's easy to set very specific goals."

00:03:23.430 --> 00:03:25.290
And like, you can watch
yourself achieve them.

00:03:25.290 --> 00:03:27.780
And I think, also there's
a really good community

00:03:27.780 --> 00:03:31.140
of non-binary and fem people who lift,

00:03:31.140 --> 00:03:33.990
who are really focused on reclaiming,

00:03:33.990 --> 00:03:36.810
not just body positivity,
but body neutrality

00:03:36.810 --> 00:03:37.643
and being like,

00:03:37.643 --> 00:03:38.940
"This is my body, and
it does things for me."

00:03:38.940 --> 00:03:40.230
And, that's awesome.

00:03:40.230 --> 00:03:44.220
- I got into lifting after I
came back home from college.

00:03:44.220 --> 00:03:45.960
All my friends were working out at a gym,

00:03:45.960 --> 00:03:47.730
at Crunch like, "Oh, we're gonna do that.

00:03:47.730 --> 00:03:49.140
'Cause I have all this time now."

00:03:49.140 --> 00:03:50.910
And then, I still continue to lift

00:03:50.910 --> 00:03:52.500
because my job requires it.

00:03:52.500 --> 00:03:55.980
And, also, because I feel more
empowered and independent.

00:03:55.980 --> 00:03:57.450
- So I started lifting...

00:03:57.450 --> 00:03:59.400
Well, I was always... Grew up athletic.

00:03:59.400 --> 00:04:02.100
I played basketball and sports,
but when I got into college

00:04:02.100 --> 00:04:04.950
I kind of started going down a dark path

00:04:04.950 --> 00:04:07.470
and I was starting to
have an eating disorder,

00:04:07.470 --> 00:04:09.510
to the point where I was eating

00:04:09.510 --> 00:04:11.623
one meal a day and then... Sorry.

00:04:11.623 --> 00:04:13.050
I don't wanna get emotional.

00:04:13.050 --> 00:04:14.070
- That's okay.

00:04:14.070 --> 00:04:16.020
- It got to the point where I was like,

00:04:16.020 --> 00:04:19.560
even like bulimic, but
weight lifting has...

00:04:19.560 --> 00:04:21.030
Sorry, I'm nervous.

00:04:21.030 --> 00:04:22.239
- You can deep breath.

00:04:22.239 --> 00:04:23.899
- It's okay. it's very emotional
to talk about these things.

00:04:23.899 --> 00:04:25.860
Yeah, 'cause I don't talk
about this with anybody.

00:04:25.860 --> 00:04:29.280
But, weightlifting has
given me a positive outlet,

00:04:29.280 --> 00:04:31.770
for me to take care of my
body in a positive way.

00:04:31.770 --> 00:04:33.180
'Cause it's hard being a girl

00:04:33.180 --> 00:04:35.760
and just every aspect of your life

00:04:35.760 --> 00:04:38.370
is just predicated on how you look.

00:04:38.370 --> 00:04:39.203
- Yeah.

00:04:39.203 --> 00:04:40.110
- Like pretty privilege is a thing.

00:04:40.110 --> 00:04:41.078
So, yeah...

00:04:41.078 --> 00:04:42.810
(supportive chatter)

00:04:42.810 --> 00:04:43.770
I was really nervous to say that.

00:04:43.770 --> 00:04:44.603
- Thank you.

00:04:44.603 --> 00:04:46.260
- Thank you guys for being so supportive.

00:04:46.260 --> 00:04:48.900
I didn't think I would get
that nervous talking about it.

00:04:48.900 --> 00:04:49.733
- How about you guys?

00:04:49.733 --> 00:04:53.340
- So I was one of those people
that walked the mile in PE.

00:04:53.340 --> 00:04:54.173
- Yes.

00:04:54.173 --> 00:04:56.370
- But, it wasn't until the summer

00:04:56.370 --> 00:04:59.640
of my senior year of high
school where a friend

00:04:59.640 --> 00:05:01.800
of mine, who is really
getting into lifting,

00:05:01.800 --> 00:05:03.630
brought a group of us over to the gym.

00:05:03.630 --> 00:05:06.990
And I remember I was having trouble

00:05:06.990 --> 00:05:09.960
with just the bar, and
just the bar is 45 pounds.

00:05:09.960 --> 00:05:11.820
Now here I am, 10 years later.

00:05:11.820 --> 00:05:14.040
Power-lifting has opened so many doors

00:05:14.040 --> 00:05:17.190
for me where now I'm
learning snowboarding,

00:05:17.190 --> 00:05:19.680
Muay Thai, and backpacking.

00:05:19.680 --> 00:05:20.864
- I'm like, "I'm scared!"

00:05:20.864 --> 00:05:22.305
(nervous chatter)

00:05:22.305 --> 00:05:23.460
- You're gonna have to come
this way. Let's go over here.

00:05:23.460 --> 00:05:24.293
- No, no, no.

00:05:24.293 --> 00:05:26.293
- You gotta go over here.

00:05:26.293 --> 00:05:27.735
I just like learning these things,

00:05:27.735 --> 00:05:29.157
it doesn't mean I'm good at it.

00:05:29.157 --> 00:05:31.560
- And your body's able to
do it cause you're strong.

00:05:31.560 --> 00:05:32.393
- Yeah.

00:05:33.780 --> 00:05:36.990
- For me, it's kind of...
more of a sad start.

00:05:36.990 --> 00:05:40.710
My ex-boyfriend beat me
to death when I was 20...

00:05:40.710 --> 00:05:41.550
I was like 20, 21.

00:05:41.550 --> 00:05:42.870
I think, I just blocked it out.

00:05:42.870 --> 00:05:44.880
I was like 20, instead
of like running away

00:05:44.880 --> 00:05:45.870
from things that scare me,

00:05:45.870 --> 00:05:47.730
like getting hit, and all that stuff,

00:05:47.730 --> 00:05:49.927
and being cornered by men, it was like

00:05:49.927 --> 00:05:52.200
"If anyone's gonna hit me,
it's gonna be on my own terms."

00:05:52.200 --> 00:05:55.260
Right? And, so it kind of went
from that, started lifting.

00:05:55.260 --> 00:05:57.120
I was like, "I'm actually kind of strong."

00:05:57.120 --> 00:05:58.598
- You're a bad (beep), dude.

00:05:58.598 --> 00:06:01.231
(supportive chatter)

00:06:01.231 --> 00:06:02.704
- You should be up here.

00:06:02.704 --> 00:06:03.809
- I think I'm the middle.

00:06:03.809 --> 00:06:05.890
I'm gonna humbly fit right
down in the middle, for now.

00:06:05.890 --> 00:06:08.160
- Now I have one question which would be,

00:06:08.160 --> 00:06:12.000
raise your hand, how many of
you have lifted competitively?

00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:12.833
Just you?

00:06:12.833 --> 00:06:14.400
Okay. Oh India.

00:06:14.400 --> 00:06:15.966
I feel like you gotta go this way.

00:06:15.966 --> 00:06:16.799
- All right.

00:06:16.799 --> 00:06:19.955
- But, that means you
gotta, you gotta move, too.

00:06:19.955 --> 00:06:21.363
- That way, yeah.

00:06:21.363 --> 00:06:22.911
- No, I think... I think this.

00:06:22.911 --> 00:06:23.744
- I don't know.

00:06:23.744 --> 00:06:28.442
- You're like a PhD student,
who outruns other humans.

00:06:28.442 --> 00:06:29.275
- Professional! Yes.

00:06:29.275 --> 00:06:30.570
- No, well we've been tapering,

00:06:30.570 --> 00:06:32.703
so I've not lifted in like a month.

00:06:33.690 --> 00:06:35.394
- I'm gonna... I just... I really...

00:06:35.394 --> 00:06:37.350
I really believe.

00:06:37.350 --> 00:06:39.512
- Okay. You've worked
your way back down there.

00:06:39.512 --> 00:06:40.440
(laughter)

00:06:40.440 --> 00:06:42.302
I dunno how I feel about that.

00:06:42.302 --> 00:06:44.220
(evil cackling)

00:06:44.220 --> 00:06:45.210
- Yeah. Let's lock it in.

00:06:45.210 --> 00:06:46.043
- This is our...

00:06:49.410 --> 00:06:51.390
- Have you done a deadlift before?

00:06:51.390 --> 00:06:53.010
- Not seriously.

00:06:53.010 --> 00:06:54.105
- Not seriously? Okay.

00:06:54.105 --> 00:06:54.938
- Hold on.

00:06:54.938 --> 00:06:55.771
- You go closer.

00:06:55.771 --> 00:06:56.670
- All right.

00:06:56.670 --> 00:06:58.680
- So yeah, I would just go hips

00:06:58.680 --> 00:07:00.774
width apart, just to start, first.

00:07:00.774 --> 00:07:01.607
- Okay.

00:07:01.607 --> 00:07:02.440
- Okay

00:07:02.440 --> 00:07:03.273
- It's gonna be a little harder

00:07:03.273 --> 00:07:05.970
'cause the bar is not
raised by the weight.

00:07:05.970 --> 00:07:06.900
- Okay. There you go.

00:07:06.900 --> 00:07:08.520
- Keep the weight in your heels, too.

00:07:08.520 --> 00:07:09.418
- Yeah.

00:07:09.418 --> 00:07:10.251
- There you go.

00:07:10.251 --> 00:07:12.319
- That looks pretty good!

00:07:12.319 --> 00:07:16.258
(encouraging chatter)

00:07:16.258 --> 00:07:18.362
- I've been pretending this
entire time. (sarcastically)

00:07:18.362 --> 00:07:19.710
- Do you wanna do 185?

00:07:19.710 --> 00:07:20.543
- You okay with that?

00:07:20.543 --> 00:07:21.376
- Let's do it!

00:07:21.376 --> 00:07:22.530
- I like this! She's like, "Let's do it!"

00:07:22.530 --> 00:07:23.430
- Now guys. I'm game.

00:07:23.430 --> 00:07:24.960
- She's got a secret, actually.

00:07:24.960 --> 00:07:27.347
- Okay, we've gotta hype
her up properly then.

00:07:27.347 --> 00:07:28.692
- Really good.

00:07:28.692 --> 00:07:29.525
- Oh my God.

00:07:29.525 --> 00:07:30.358
- Let's go girl!

00:07:30.358 --> 00:07:31.441
- I'm hazing.

00:07:32.655 --> 00:07:33.635
- Let's go.

00:07:33.635 --> 00:07:34.468
- I believe in you!

00:07:34.468 --> 00:07:37.080
- Remember, drag it up.
Push through your feet.

00:07:37.080 --> 00:07:38.370
- Yeah, there you go.

00:07:38.370 --> 00:07:39.203
- Let's go, let's go.

00:07:39.203 --> 00:07:40.036
- Stay tight.

00:07:41.040 --> 00:07:43.454
- There we go. You got this.

00:07:43.454 --> 00:07:46.452
(excited cheering)

00:07:46.452 --> 00:07:47.461
- I love it.

00:07:47.461 --> 00:07:48.685
- You didn't even flinch!

00:07:48.685 --> 00:07:49.880
(excited chatter)

00:07:49.880 --> 00:07:51.495
- Yeah! You did pretty freaking good!

00:07:51.495 --> 00:07:52.530
- I thought I was gonna lift it once,

00:07:52.530 --> 00:07:54.000
and that was gonna be it.

00:07:54.000 --> 00:07:54.833
- Do you have enough chalk on your hands?

00:07:54.833 --> 00:07:55.778
- Go closer, closer.

00:07:55.778 --> 00:07:57.510
(energetic music)

00:07:57.510 --> 00:07:58.380
- You got this!

00:07:58.380 --> 00:07:59.358
Perfect.

00:07:59.358 --> 00:08:00.191
You got it. Let's go.

00:08:00.191 --> 00:08:01.130
- Plant those feet. You got it.

00:08:02.062 --> 00:08:03.700
(proud cheering)

00:08:03.700 --> 00:08:05.927
(bell dings)

00:08:05.927 --> 00:08:08.177
(applause)

00:08:10.500 --> 00:08:12.570
- Bre, I'm so proud of her!

00:08:12.570 --> 00:08:15.300
- Like I can't believe
she never lifted before.

00:08:15.300 --> 00:08:18.660
- I hope this like inspires
her to like try it out.

00:08:18.660 --> 00:08:19.860
- It was invigorating.

00:08:19.860 --> 00:08:20.693
I will say.

00:08:20.693 --> 00:08:22.230
And I think I would try it again.

00:08:22.230 --> 00:08:23.063
I'm not crying.

00:08:23.063 --> 00:08:24.585
There's sweat in my eyes.

00:08:24.585 --> 00:08:26.062
(laughter)

00:08:26.062 --> 00:08:26.913
- Yeah, you got this!

00:08:26.913 --> 00:08:28.864
- Let's go, let's go! Big breath.

00:08:28.864 --> 00:08:30.027
- Hey, come on, you got it!

00:08:30.027 --> 00:08:30.930
- You got it.

00:08:30.930 --> 00:08:33.497
(encouraging cheers)

00:08:33.497 --> 00:08:34.879
(proud cheering)

00:08:34.879 --> 00:08:37.022
(bell dings)

00:08:37.022 --> 00:08:39.930
- You frigging did it! Oh my God!

00:08:39.930 --> 00:08:41.635
- That's a PR?

00:08:41.635 --> 00:08:42.495
(applause)

00:08:42.495 --> 00:08:43.328
- Holy cow!

00:08:43.328 --> 00:08:44.161
- That's so cool.

00:08:44.161 --> 00:08:44.994
- That's a lot of weight.

00:08:44.994 --> 00:08:47.350
- I don't even know if
